#include \(dqserver.h\(dq

int protocol_read_line(int fd, char *buf, size_t bufsize);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads a single line from the file descriptor \f[CR]fd\f[R], terminated
by a newline character (\f[CR]\(rsn\f[R]).
The trailing newline is stripped and not stored in \f[CR]buf\f[R].
Carriage return characters (\f[CR]\(rsr\f[R]) are silently discarded,
allowing the function to handle both LF and CRLF line endings
transparently.
.PP
Reading proceeds one byte at a time via \f[CR]read(2)\f[R].
If \f[CR]EINTR\f[R] is received, the read is retried automatically.
Reading stops when a newline is encountered, EOF is reached (with at
least one byte already buffered), or the buffer is full
(\f[CR]bufsize \- 1\f[R] bytes stored).
.PP
The result is always NUL\-terminated.
.PP
This function is used for the v1 text protocol.
For v2 framed I/O, see \f[CR]json_frame_read(3)\f[R].
