.PP
The recommended buffer size is \f[CR]SERVER_MAX_LINE\f[R] (8192 bytes),
which is the maximum line length defined by the v1 protocol.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, returns the number of bytes stored in \f[CR]buf\f[R]
(excluding the NUL terminator).
A return value of 0 indicates an empty line (bare \f[CR]\(rsn\f[R]).
.PP
Returns \f[B]\-1\f[R] on error or if EOF is encountered with no bytes
buffered.
.SH ERRORS
Returns \-1 when:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]read(2)\f[R] fails with an error other than \f[CR]EINTR\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
EOF is reached before any data has been read into \f[CR]buf\f[R].
.PP
The function does \f[B]not\f[R] set \f[CR]errno\f[R] itself; the value
left by \f[CR]read(2)\f[R] is preserved on error.
